Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I was wondering if it's possible to retrieve the filtering status of a DataTable.  I want to be able to know the exact state of a dataset being rendered in a DataTable, so if the user clicked on one of the columns to sort by that variable or if the user entered a filter string into some of the filter boxes underneath, I want to know that as well.

Does anyone know how to do that?

Thanks!

Example ui.R:
library(shiny)
shinyUI(fluidPage(fluidRow(
 actionButton("actionBtn", "What's in the table?"),
 textOutput("output"), br(),
  dataTableOutput(outputId = "table")
)))

Example server.R:
library(shiny)
shinyServer(function(input, output) {
 output$table <- renderDataTable({
 iris
 })
 output$output <- renderText({
 input$actionBtn

 paste0("Table parameters: ???")
 })
})

