Hello,

I posted this question to stackoverflow, but repeating it here because it really is most usefull in the context of Shiny apps. Here's a link to the post, and the content copied below:

http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27001528/r-source-url-get-url-from-within-the-script

I am creating library functions within subversion (with trunk and tag subfolders) on a web server behind our corporate firewall. In this setup I would like to make a call like:

source('http://server.com/lib/trunk/lib_file.R')

But it may also get used as:

source('http://server.com/lib/tags/version1/lib_file.R')

so from within lib_file.R how may I find out what URL was used to source it?

