Hi all,

I have the following situation:
- I have a datatable (sortable)
- when I click on a row, I want to subset the data and allow for data entry.
- based on the data entry I want to update the original table.

Code below is the smallest, simplified example of what I want to achieve.  In this case, based on the selection of a row, I want to udpate the width for the full table.

ui.R
library(shiny)
shinyUI(fluidPage(
    fluidRow(
      column(5, dataTableOutput('tbl'))
      ,column(7, htmlOutput('length'))
  )))

Server.R
library(shiny)
shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {
  output$tbl <- renderDataTable({
        iris$Sepal.Width <- input$value
        return(iris)},
        callback = "function(table) {
          table.on('click.dt', 'tr', function() {
            Shiny.onInputChange('value',table.data()[$(this).index()][0]);
          });
        }"
  )

  output$length <- renderText({
     paste(c('Length:', input$value), collapse = ' ')
  })
})

The issue I have with this, that the sorting is thrown away each time I click on a line.

Any advice?

Thanks,
Tom

